       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day for adults. At that dose the risks include serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation, and severe GI or bleeding effects. Kidney and liver function being normal doesn't change that.\n\nWas this a typo? Typical adult dosing is:\n- **Depression, OCD, or PTSD:** start at 25\u201350 mg daily and titrate up to 200 mg daily.\n- **Panic disorder or social anxiety:** start at 25 mg daily, then 50 mg, and titrate up to 200 mg.\n\nIf you meant something like 50 mg or 100 mg daily, tell me the dose and I'll enter it right away. If you do intend 600 mg, for example as a deliberate off-label choice, please confirm that and give me a short rationale to add to the order note. I'd also suggest pharmacy review before it's entered."
